        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The first ’d means would; the second ’d means had." data-hint="Use the following forms: base call after the first contraction and participle sent after the second." data-fix="In she’d call, ’d means would; in she’d sent, ’d means had."><p class="quiz-question">5. What does <span class="ex">’d</span> mean in <span class="ex">she’d call</span> and <span class="ex">she’d sent</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The first ’d means would; the second ’d means had.">The first ’d means would; the second ’d means had.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both contractions mean did.">Both contractions mean did.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both contractions mean should.">Both contractions mean should.</button></div></div>
