      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details>
      <summary>Tutor transcript and evidence notes</summary>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="ex">Mina TOLD Alex that the TRAIN was deLAYED.</span> Evidence: <span class="ex">told + listener Alex + clause</span>.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">Mina said she was running LATE.</span> Evidence: original present temporary state viewed through a later past report.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">She said her train had been CANceled that MORning.</span> Evidence: Past Perfect explicitly places cancellation before the report.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">She said she would CALL the NEXT DAY.</span> Evidence: original future relative to the message becomes <span class="ex">would</span> plus adjusted day.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">She’d CALL on Tuesday. She’d SENT the form on Monday.</span> Evidence: base <span class="ex">call</span> resolves <span class="ex">’d</span> as <span class="ex">would</span>; participle <span class="ex">sent</span> resolves it as <span class="ex">had</span>.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
